 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official AWSMainframeModernization API (2021-04-28). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Applications are stored records: no runtime environment, deployment, listener, load balancer, batch job, data set, log group or BluInsights session exists, so every application stays Created with no environment, no deployed version and no endpoint. Environments, deployments, StartApplication, StopApplication, StartBatchJob, data set import and export, application versions, GetSignedBluinsightsUrl and every other official operation return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. The application definition is validated and then discarded because GetApplicationVersion is not implemented: exactly one of content (a JSON object) or s3Location must be given, the S3 object is never read, and definitionContent is never returned. UpdateApplication creates the next version number and reports it as latestVersion, but only that number, its creation time and the status Available are stored. UpdateApplication refuses a currentApplicationVersion other than the latest version with ConflictException (the simulator's reading of the documented current version of the application to update). ListApplications supports the environmentId filter, which never matches because no application has an environment; the names filter is refused instead of being ignored. The applicationId is a 10 character simulator identifier. Names must be unique within the Region as a local limit, and at most 50 applications exist per Region. DeleteApplication does not model ResourceNotFoundException, so deleting a missing application fails with ValidationException.",
  "title": "AWS Mainframe Modernization (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2021-04-28"
 },
